  <!-- The large scale MS decoders, split out of Zimo_MS_small_v4.xml, which despite its name
       carried MS950 and MS990. They differ from the small ones in more than size: variable low
       voltage (CV264), high voltage RailCom (CV28 bit 6), 14 or 15 function outputs, smoke
       generator connections and more servo and switch inputs.
       The family name is deliberately unchanged, so existing roster entries keep resolving -
       a family spanning several files is normal (Zimo Unified software spans 82). -->

  <!-- Version identification: CV #7 is the main software version and CV #65 the sub-version, so
       the version 4 families are gated to CV #7 = 4 exactly while these run 5 to 42. The 42 is
       deliberate, not a leftover - it keeps one open-ended family so a future 6.x decoder still
       identifies as something if the definitions have not caught up. The open end moves to the
       newest generation each time. -->

